Problem 1:
Write a Name Class that stores the first name, middle initial and last name. The first and last names are stored as CString (null terminated character arrays) and middle initial is stored as a character. Write the code for the class, both specification and implementation, so that the following main program executes successfully.

	void print(Name _name){
		cout << “Inside doSomething “ << _name << endl;
	}

int main(){
    Name name1(“Object”, ‘O’, “Programming”);
    cout << name1 << endl;		//It prints Object O. Programming
    print(name1);  
    cout << name1 << endl;

    return 0;
}

(Note: Write only the required functions. No extra function is allowed.)

